WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:08.526
Ask anybody around you this simple question:

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:09.760
“What is gravity?”

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.160
And what you’d probably hear is

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.850
“it’s something that pulls objects towards the earth”

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.520
or “it’s a force exerted by the earth

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.430
to pull objects towards it”.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.937
Now before we get to the basics of gravitation,

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:23.230
there is one thing I want you to understand

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.230
well.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.880
Rather there’s one thing I want you to forget!

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.960
Forget the fact that gravity has got to do

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.180
ONLY with the earth and the objects close

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.180
to it.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.829
That’s NOT gravity!

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:37.960
We’d see examples where objects are falling

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.819
to the ground and we assume that it’s the

00:00:39.819 --> 00:00:42.230
only concept we need to know about gravity.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.007
Yes of course its gravity that pulls the objects

00:00:45.007 --> 00:00:47.379
towards the earth but that’s NOT the only

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:50.719
thing you need to understand about gravity!

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:52.190
So what is gravity?

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:55.320
Consider your screen to be the Universe.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.699
And these are any two objects in the universe.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.540
They could be planets or humans

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.459
or animals or whatever.

00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:06.549
Just that they both have non-zero mass!

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:09.206
In this case, both objects are pulling the

00:01:09.206 --> 00:01:11.230
other object towards each other.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.530
This object is pulling this one towards itself.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.190
And the other object is pulling this one towards itself.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.460
This attractive force between any two masses

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.440
in the universe is called the

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.860
 

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.660
 

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.720
It’s not ONLY the force that earth uses

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.100
to pull objects towards it!

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.820
But yes, as all of us have earth as our habitat,

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.970
most examples we see for gravitation will

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.110
relate to the earth pulling objects towards it.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.140
But you should know that it’s not the only

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.000
force that explains gravitation.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.240
In the case of earth and a human being, the

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.520
earth is one object and the human being is

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.460
another.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.440
Both are pulling the other towards themselves.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.040
But why does this happen?

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.820
If you do a lot of research in to what gravity

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:07.220
really means, you may find out that gravity is

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:10.960
not actually a force and it’s just an illusion

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.775
So for now, it’s enough to know that gravitational

00:02:13.775 --> 00:02:16.140
force is just the attractive force between

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.140
any two objects with non-zero mass separated

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.700
by a distance.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.800
After knowing the basics, you’d probably

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.139
have many questions in mind.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.300
Does the apple fall towards the earth or does

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.320
the earth move towards the apple?

00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:31.920
If two objects always attract each other,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.970
why don’t two humans get pulled towards

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:35.970
each other?

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.849
Why don’t two stars collide with each other?

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:41.455
After watching our videos based on Gravitation

00:02:41.455 --> 00:02:44.060
you will be able to answer all these questions

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.469
and understand various concepts related to them!

00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:48.200
Happy Learning!

